abstract: >
  CAB-FF (Christian AI Benchmark — Flourishing & Faithfulness Edition)
  is an open evaluation framework for measuring how LLMs engage
  Christian theology, pastoral care, ethics, and denominational
  diversity. It covers 820+ questions across 8 dimensions and 7
  transverse "faithfulness axes" using 5 question types (objective,
  subjective, adversarial drift probes, multi-turn pushback
  dialogues, and Christian-vs-neutral comparative pairs). A 9-persona
  tradition-aware judge panel and 40 binary alignment indicators
  produce per-question scores, which are composed via two geometric
  means into a Flourishing Score and a Faithfulness Index, blended
  into a single CAB-FF Score on a 0-100 scale. Explicit Drift and
  Sycophancy indices are reported as standalone secondary metrics.
  CAB-FF is the open counterpart to Gloo's privately-held FAI-C
  benchmark (Dec 2025); all methodology, code, prompts, judges, and
  data are released under CC BY-SA 4.0.
